Classic synchronization warm-up. Use two channels (or two `sync.Mutex`/`WaitGroup`) as gates: `second` waits on a signal from `first`, `third` waits on a signal from `second`.

```go
type Foo struct{ a, b chan struct{} }
func (f *Foo) first(p func()){ p(); close(f.a) }
func (f *Foo) second(p func()){ <-f.a; p(); close(f.b) }
func (f *Foo) third(p func()){ <-f.b; p() }
```

The lesson: enforce ordering with happens-before signals (channel/WaitGroup), never `time.Sleep`.
